      "text": "$2x+7=3$\n$2x=-4$\n$x=-2$\n\n$bx-10=-2$\n$b=-2\\times x+10=2+10=12$\n\n$\\boxed{12}$\n\nThe graphs of $r = 4 \\cos \\theta$ and $r = 8 \\sin \\theta$ intersect at two points.  Find the distance between these two points.\n\nSolution:\nEach equation can be written in rectangular coordinates as\n\n[asy]\ndraw((16,0)--(8,sqrt(2))*--(4,sqrt(3))*--(0,sqrt(2))*--(-4,sqrt(3))*--(-8,-sqrt(2))*--(-16,0));\ndraw((8,-sqrt(2)/4)+ (8,0)*dir(135)--(8,0)*dir(45));\nlabel(\"$(8,-\\sqrt{2})$\", (8,0), dir(45));\nlabel(\"$(8, \\sqrt{2})$\", (8,0), dir(135));\ndraw( (-16,0)--(-8,-sqrt(2))*--(-4,-sqrt(3))*--(0,-sqrt(2))*--(4,-sqrt(3))*--(8,-sqrt(2))*--(16,0));\ndraw((16,0)--(8,0)*dir(225)--(8,8)--(16,0)*dir(315));\nlabel(\"$(16,0)$\", (16,0), dir(225));\nlabel(\"$(8,0)$\", (8,0), dir(315));\nlabel(\"$y=\\cos x$\",(-2*sqrt(2),16/3),S);\nlabel(\"$y=\\sin x$\",(16/3,-2*sqrt(2)),SW);\nlabel(\"$r$\",(-8,-sqrt(2)),SW);\nlabel(\"$r=$\",(-8,-sqrt(2))/2,S);\ndot((4,sqrt(3)));\ndot((-4,sqrt(3)));\ndot((-4,-sqrt(3)));\ndot((8,-sqrt(2)));\ndot((1,1.5));\ndot((-1,1.5));\n[/asy]\n\nBlacklo ship movement\nThe x-intercepts of the circle given by $y = \\cos x$ are $(0,1)$ and $(2\\pi,1)$, and the x-intercepts of the circle given by $y = \\sin x$ are $(0,-1)$ and $(-2\\pi,-1)$. The points of intersection must lie on the $x$-axis, so the two points of intersection are $(0,1)$ and $(0,-1)$.\nThe distance between the two points is $1 - (-1) = \\boxed{2}$.\nThe answer is: 2",
