      "text": "Given the equations:\n1. $2x+7=3$\n2. $bx-10=-2$\n\nStep 1: We solve the first equation for $x$.\nWe start with $2x+7=3$.\nSubtracting $7$ from both sides gives $2x=-4$.\nDividing by $2$ on both sides results in $x=-2$.\n\nStep 2: Since both equations have the same solution, $x$, we substitute $x=-2$ into the second equation.\nThe second equation is $bx-10=-2$.\nSubstituting $x=-2$ gives us $b(-2)-10=-2$.\n\nStep 3: Adjust the equation to solve for $b$.\n$-2b-10=-2$\nAdding $10$ to both sides gives $-2b=8$. \nFinally, we divide by $-2$ on both sides to get $b=-4$.\n\nSo the value of $b$ is $\\boxed{-4}$.",
